                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Beside the tempo figure, \u00f72 and \u00d72 read the loop as half or twice its bars, at half or twice the tempo, the audio as it is (#1936, decision D4). They are live only when the engine would apply them: a tempo derived from the loop and not retimed since, whole bars, one shared loop (not Free or Song), no take recording and no count-in; halving needs an even bar count, and the tempo stays in 30 to 300 BPM. Otherwise they are dimmed, as here with no derived tempo shown. The tempo figure scales down to leave them room. The same two buttons sit on the main screen's Tempo & click page, after the 1 BPM and 0.01 BPM steps. The beat analysis already chose the bar count when the first take closed (power-of-two bars at 60 to 200 BPM, else nearest 120); these are the correction when it chose the wrong octave."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
